 on the bf16 logits they produce, and remaps the"," selected columns back to request-local positions."," ","-Only the MXFP4 indexer cache is supported: the kernels require UE8M0-packed","-(granularity-32) Q/KV scales, which is exactly the MXFP4 cache layout. The","-FP8 indexer cache stores one fp32 scale per quant block instead.","+The kernels take UE8M0-packed (granularity-32) Q/KV scales, which both","+indexer caches provide on SM100: MXFP4 stores them natively, and the FP8 cache","+stores each token's power-of-two scale as four equal UE8M0 bytes (MXFP8 with","+one shared scale). FP8 Q carries its per-(token, head) scale in the weights,","+so it is passed with unit UE8M0 scales, as on the dense path. The Q dtype","+(MXFP4 viewed as int8, or FP8 e4m3) selects the kernel variant."," "," The functions here take caller-owned output buffers (``sparse_indices``,"," ``end``, ``col_indices``) so the hot path allocates nothing; the indexer","@@ -331,9 +334,9 @@ def sparse_mqa_logits_prefill_chunk(","     \"\"\"Sparse-MQA logits + top-k for one prefill chunk (packed KV workspace)."," ","     Args:","-        q: [rows, H, D] packed Q values (MXFP4 viewed as int8).","+        q: [rows, H, D] Q values (MXFP4 viewed as int8, or FP8 e4m3).","         q_scale: [rows, H] int32 packed UE8M0 Q scales.","-        k_quant: [total_kv, D] packed K workspace (MXFP4 viewed as int8).","+        k_quant: [total_kv, D] K workspace, same dtype as ``q``.","         k_scale: [total_kv] int32 packed UE8M0 K scales.","         weights: [rows, H] bf16 per-head weights; the sparse kernels take","             bf16 and do not fold the Q scale in.","@@ -424,7 +427,7 @@ def sparse_mqa_logits_paged_decode(","     builder), so ``block_table`` is already per row."," ","     Args:","-        q: [rows, 1, H, D] packed Q values (MXFP4 viewed as int8).","+        q: [rows, 1, H, D] Q values (MXFP4 viewed as int8, or FP8 e4m3).","         q_scale: [rows, 1, H] int32 packed UE8M0 Q scales.","         kv_cache: 